# Signing keys, certificates, and store credentials — NEVER commit.
#
# This repository is intended to be made public (see README "Status"), so
# a key committed here is a key published to the world, and rewriting
# history after the fact does not un-publish it. Treat these patterns as
# a backstop: the keys belong in a password manager or CI secret store,
# not in the working tree at all.
#
#   .p8              App Store Connect API key, In-App Purchase key.
#                    Apple lets you download these exactly ONCE, which is
#                    precisely why they get parked somewhere convenient.
#   .p12 / .cer      exported signing certificates, .p12 includes the
#                    private key
#   .mobileprovision provisioning profiles (embed team id + device list)
#
# Android upload keystores and key.properties are already covered by
# client/android/.gitignore.
*.p8
*.p12
*.cer
*.mobileprovision

# Web
client/web/build/

# Provability artifacts produced locally (not tracked; releases are tagged)
provability/reproducible-build/out/

